    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1124">

                <pb facs="0940" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 612.1123/121.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Silliman to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s March 13. In a long conference with the First Chief, at which the
                    Secretary of Foreign Relations, Secretary of Treasury, Secretary of Gobernacion,
                    and Mr. Belt were present, General Carranza finally said that he would accede to
                    the wish of the American Government and recall his order closing the port of
                    Progreso. I was not obliged to communicate in any way the President’s
                    intentions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
